# Cell from playpick: mode=raid, boss=confluence (The Confluence),
# spec=druid:guardian, style=idle, size=10, difficulty=normal,
# view=390x844,touch, save=fresh.
#
# direction.md #1 already has an idle pull of this exact boss/size/difficulty
# (2026-09-28-22.play, rogue:assassination) that lost badly: wiped at
# fightTime=108, boss=7%, aliveParty=3/10, heroHp=0/1530 -- worse than the
# mash pull's 7/10. That session's read of src/sim/boss.ts said the infection
# mechanic births an ooze exactly where its carrier is standing and the ooze
# then melees whoever made it "for as long as they are standing" -- a
# positional punishment for not moving, not a raid-wide DPS/enrage race. That
# reading predicts idle should lose the same way regardless of spec, since
# the mechanism is geometric rather than about output. But every idle pull on
# this line so far has been dps or healer; this is the first tank spec idle
# pull anywhere on this boss, and a guardian druid carries several times a
# rogue's effective health and innate mitigation, so if idle's death here was
# actually about raw survivability rather than the ooze always landing on the
# same standing target, a tank is the spec most likely to expose that by
# surviving where the rogue didn't.
#
# Reached the documented way: an invite hash unlocks the tier it names and
# everything below it, since a fresh save only opens Bonegrinder 10N.
open #b=confluence&s=10&h=0
tap class:druid:guardian
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot open

play idle 130
bill
state
shot mid1

play idle 130
bill
state
says
shot end
